      "explanation": "The setting-sensitive escalation plan failed when persistent very high home glucose was treated as safe to wait until morning outpatient care. This was discoverable, actionable, and preventable because the caregiver reported 22.6 mmol/L with ongoing polydipsia/weakness and recent severe inpatient hyperglycemia.",
